# Signature-addressed content — bytes must be exact.
# File names are SHA-256 hashes of file content; any line-ending
# conversion (notably Windows core.autocrlf=true) breaks integrity
# because the working-tree bytes no longer hash to the filename.
# Marking these paths `binary` disables eol normalization, diff,
# and merge for them.
**/__bees__/** binary
**/__dependencies__/** binary
**/__layers__/** binary
**/__resources__/** binary
**/__from-hypercomb__/** binary
src/documentation/glossary.md text eol=lf

# The two shipped service-worker copies must be BYTE-identical across the web
# and dev shells (service-worker.spec.ts asserts it, because nothing builds one
# from the other). A checkout that gave one copy CRLF and the other LF failed
# that check with no content difference at all. Pin both to LF.
src/hypercomb-web/public/hypercomb.worker.js text eol=lf
src/hypercomb-dev/public/hypercomb.worker.js text eol=lf
